    "python-kwargs-casing": {
      "statement": "The Python SDK takes snake_case keyword arguments and camelCases the whole request body before sending; an explicit exception table makes `show_eun`, `show_eunatp`, `min_tls_version`, `min_client_tls_version` and `min_server_tls_version` become the contract spellings, so jq queries on snapshot data must use the camelCase names.",
      "tier": "A",
      "conditions": "The jq statement is advice following from the wire being camelCase; snapshot data comes from the API, not from the Python SDK.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "sdk-python",
          "path": "zscaler/helpers.py",
          "quotes": [
            "\"show_eun\": \"showEUN\",",
            "\"show_eunatp\": \"showEUNATP\",",
            "\"min_client_tls_version\": \"minClientTLSVersion\","
          ]
        },
        {
          "source": "sdk-python",
          "path": "zscaler/request_executor.py",
          "quotes": [
            "body = convert_keys_to_camel_case(body)"
          ],
          "after": "# Preserve existing logic for other services"
        }
      ]
    },
    "python-no-client-validation": {
      "statement": "Apart from key and ID rewriting, the Python SDK sends the caller's keyword arguments as the request body without checking the action: `add_rule` assigns `body = kwargs`, so a `decryptSubActions` block on a `DO_NOT_DECRYPT` rule, or any of the combinations the Go SDK rejects, reaches the API unchecked.",
      "tier": "A",
      "conditions": "Code read: no validation step appears between kwargs and the request. What the API itself does with such a body is gap zia.sdk-go.service-defects:ssl-action-api-contract.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "sdk-python",
          "path": "zscaler/zia/ssl_inspection_rules.py",
          "quotes": [
            "body = kwargs"
          ],
          "after": "Adds a new ssl inspection filter rule."
        }
      ],
      "gaps": [
        "zia.sdk-go.service-defects:ssl-action-api-contract"
      ]
    },
    "go-validator-block-and-cert-rules": {
      "statement": "Beyond the required-field rules recorded in the SDK defects, the Go validator also rejects a `DECRYPT` rule that sets `showEUN` or `showEUNATP`, a `BLOCK` rule that carries either sub-action block or sets `showEUNATP`, and any rule with `overrideDefaultCertificate` false that attaches `sslInterceptionCert`.",
      "tier": "A",
      "binds": [
        "zia/ssl-inspection-rules#action",
        "zia/ssl-inspection-rules#action.sslInterceptionCert"
      ],
      "conditions": "Client-side checks only; whether the API enforces the same rules is gap zia.sdk-go.service-defects:ssl-action-api-contract.",
